### Risk Limit Bars — value vs limit with utilization
```tsx
import { LimitBar } from "@unified-trading/ui-kit";

// Green < 70%, amber 70-90%, red > 90%
<LimitBar
  label="Delta Exposure"
  value={2.4}
  limit={5.0}
  unit="$m"
  showTimeSeries  // toggle to see utilization over time
/>
// Renders: Delta Exposure  ████████████░░░░░  $2.4m / $5.0m  (48%)  ● healthy

<LimitBar
  label="Margin (Binance)"
  value={78}
  limit={80}
  unit="%"
/>
// Renders: Margin (Binance)  █████████████████░  78% / 80%  (97%)  ▲ WARNING
```

## Temporal Patterns (Snapshot + Time Series)

Every view that shows state must support the global `AsOfDatetime` picker.

### Point-in-time snapshot (the "time machine")
```tsx
import { useAsOfDatetime } from "@unified-trading/ui-kit";

function PositionsPage() {
  const { asOf, isLive } = useAsOfDatetime();
  // asOf = Date | null (null = live)
  // isLive = true when viewing real-time data

  const positions = useQuery({
    queryKey: ["positions", asOf?.toISOString()],
    queryFn: () => fetchPositions({ as_of: asOf }),
    refetchInterval: isLive ? 5000 : false, // Only poll when live
  });
}
```

**URL state:** `?as_of=2026-03-14T14:32:00Z` — omitted means live. All API calls pass this param.

### Time series (embedded inline)
```tsx
import { TimeSeriesToggle, TimeSeriesChart } from "@unified-trading/ui-kit";

function PnLCard({ value, componentKey }) {
  const [showTimeSeries, setShowTimeSeries] = useState(false);

  return (
    <div>
      <div className="stat-value">{value}</div>
      <TimeSeriesToggle active={showTimeSeries} onChange={setShowTimeSeries} />
      {showTimeSeries && (
        <TimeSeriesChart
          metric={componentKey}
          periods={["1d", "1w", "1m", "3m", "1y"]}
          defaultPeriod="1w"
        />
      )}
    </div>
  );
}
```

### What gets snapshot + time series

| Data Domain | Snapshot (as-of T) | Time Series (over period) |
|---|---|---|
| Positions | Exact positions at T | Position size evolution, entry/exit markers |
| P&L | Cumulative P&L at T, attribution at T | Equity curve, daily bars, component evolution |
| Risk / Exposure | Delta/funding/basis/greeks at T | Exposure drift, margin util trend, LTV evolution |
| Alerts | Active alerts at T | Alert frequency, resolution time trends |
| Strategy Status | Live/paused/killed at T | Lifecycle timeline (promoted, paused, killed) |
| Feature Freshness | SLA compliance at T | Freshness degradation, breach history |
| Orders / Fills | Orders in flight at T | Order flow over time, fill rate |

**Rule:** Every KPI card shows a sparkline of that metric over time. Every table has a "show over time" toggle.

## Performance Patterns

- **Memoize expensive computations**: `useMemo` for filtered/sorted grid data
- **Virtualize long lists**: Use `@tanstack/react-virtual` for 1000+ row grids (DimensionalGrid)
- **Debounce search/filter**: 300ms debounce on FilterBar text inputs
- **URL state over React state**: Filters in query params (survives refresh, shareable, no state sync bugs)
- **Lazy load routes**: `React.lazy()` for non-landing pages (split per surface section)

## DO

- Use AppShell for every UI — never build a custom shell
- Use EntityLink for every entity name in every table
- Use globals.css tokens — never hardcode colors
- Put new shared components in ui-kit, never in individual UI repos
- Use JetBrains Mono for numeric data (prices, PnL, quantities, timestamps)
- Pass `as_of` param to every API call that returns state data
- Show sparklines on every KPI card — the trajectory matters as much as the value
- Support the global AsOfDatetimePicker in every surface that shows positions, P&L, or risk
- Only poll/stream when `isLive=true` — historical views are static fetches

## NEVER

- Import from one UI repo into another (use ui-kit as the shared layer)
- Hardcode port numbers — use SurfaceRegistry
- Build a view that only works in "live" mode — every state view must accept ?as_of=
- Show a number without its sparkline trajectory (P&L, positions, risk metrics)
- Use white/light backgrounds (dark theme is canonical)
- Create a new color that isn't in the token system
- Build a sidebar nav from scratch — use SidebarNav from ui-kit

